# Capture the Flag — SIMPLE pack (v1.2.1)
Minecraft Bedrock | Script API | AI-assisted

NOT an official Mojang/Microsoft product.

## What this pack is
Behavior pack for casual 1v1 / small-group Capture the Flag on **any world**.
This **SIMPLE** build does NOT place automatic banners or concrete.
You only set base coordinates with the admin stick.
Optional: place your own banners by hand for looks.

## Map
Works on any map (flat, survival, custom arenas, etc.).
If you use someone else's map, respect the author's rules.
Example arena we also tested gameplay ideas with (optional):
Airship Capture the Flag Battles:
https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft-bedrock/maps/airship-capture-the-flag-battles
This pack does NOT include that map.

## Requirements
- Minecraft Bedrock 1.21+
- Beta APIs ON (required)
- Behavior pack activated
- Hosted world (session ends when host leaves)

## Install
1. Import this .mcpack
2. Activate the behavior pack in your world
3. Enable Beta APIs
4. Enter the world

## How to play
1. First player = Host → Admin stick
2. Stand where red should score → Set red base
3. Stand where blue should score → Set blue base
4. Players pick team (Visitor stick)
5. Start match
6. Near enemy base = steal flag | near your base with flag = score
7. First to 3 points wins (Match Point at 2)

## Features
- Same core rules as the Map pack (alarm, flag weight, base resistance,
  kit, emeralds, shop, respawn, saved base coordinates)
- No automatic world editing (no concrete/banner placement)

## Warnings
- Use only ONE CTF pack (Map OR Simple, not both)
- Keep Inventory OFF recommended during matches
- Ally shop can add entities — don't spam on phones
- Achievements may be affected by Beta APIs / packs
- Updates to Minecraft may break Script API packs

